  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "Autoregressive Mosaics (AM-Bench) introduces a benchmark for assessing 2D spatial reasoning in text-only large language models, while SpatialGuard provides a structured framework for complex 3D spatial text-to-image generation.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Autoregressive Mosaics (AM-Bench) separates translation and layout tasks to determine if spatial performance is due to code generation or visual composition.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SpatialGuard uses a Visual Alignment Critic to validate spatial reasoning and introduces a Layout Harness to manage constraints across iterations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Experiments show that SpatialGuard achieves state-of-the-art performance in complex 3D spatial generation and improves spatial faithfulness compared to existing baselines.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
